t":"The coloured state shows where an industry is in its cycle: a broad sell-off (Sold off), a broad rebound (Bouncing back), an established trend (Rising together), or breadth breaking down (Losing steam)."},{"title":"Read the three bars","text":"They show the share of the industry's counted stocks above their 9, 20 and 50-day averages: the short, medium and longer trend. Long bars mean most stocks are rising together."},{"title":"Check the market","text":"The Nifty 50 against its 200-day average shows the backdrop. Industry rebounds have behaved differently in weak and strong markets."},{"title":"Open an industry","text":"See a year of its breadth, every rebound and when it faded, and how each stock has done inside it. Leader flags mark stocks at 52-week highs while their industry is still well down."}],"state_how":{"washout":"Most of the industry has been sold. Watch for it to turn: most stocks turning up together. A sell-off can last weeks, so on its own it says nothing about timing.","thrust_c":"Most of the industry's stocks turned up together after a sell-off. See whether it holds and moves on to Rising together, or turns to Losing steam.","thrust_cap":"Most of the industry's stocks turned up together after a sell-off in which almost all of them kept falling to the end. See whether it holds and moves on to Rising together, or turns to Losing steam.","confirmed":"Most of the industry's stocks are trending up together. This describes a trend already under way.","fading":"A rebound or uptrend has lost its breadth: fewer of the industry's stocks are taking part.","neutral":"None of the other states applies today. The bars show how many stocks are above their averages.","none":"Too few stocks pass the counting rules for a reading."},"disclaimer":"Describes price and breadth data for NSE industries. Not a recommendation to buy, sell or hold any security.","locked":{"leader_flags":"silver"},"plan":"basic"}